  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Tuesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Satellite shows widespread cloud cover \ntoday which will assist in keeping temperatures around ten degrees\nbelow normal today. A few isolated showers may also be able to \nform in Humboldt County but no measurable precipitation is \nexpected to reach the surface. A few isolated showers continue \nalong the northern state border due to a low pressure center \nmoving onshore in the Pacific Northwest. Winds will continue to be\nstrong, particularly in White Pine and southeast Elko Counties, \nand cloud cover will continue to restrict temperatures. The low is\nexpected to meander around the PacNW Friday and Saturday, keeping\ntemperatures lower and winds stronger. For Sunday the low is \nexpected to combine with a tropical cyclone in the Eastern Pacific\nand bring much stronger moisture into the Southwest. The extent \nof impacts from this moisture are still in flux, however shower\nand thunderstorm chances are in place across the entire forecast\narea for Sunday, with weaker storms anticipated to linger for\nearly next week.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in below normal\ntemperatures and moderate confidence in precipitation chances for\nthe next several days. Increasing confidence regarding storms this\nweekend, currently sitting around the moderate level. No changes\nto NBM output.",
